      {
        "index": 4,
        "name": "What Kami Do: Harvesting",
        "description": "MENU: \u201cAlright, time to teach you how to use your kami. My world data might be messed up but these basic mechanics shouldn\u2019t be too different, I hope.\u201d\nMENU: \u201cSo, if you open your party screen, you\u2019ll be able to see your kami is currently resting while you\u2019re holding it. Kamigotchi will rest and stay healthy when being held. Being close to an Operator seems to comfort and restore them.\u201d\nMENU: \u201cWhen you send a Kami out into a room using the Start Harvest button, they\u2019ll begin drawing the spiritual energy of the local environment into themselves.\u201d\nMENU: \u201cWe call this process Harvesting. A harvesting kami isn\u2019t working up a sweat, kami are spirits, not animals.\nMENU: \u201cThat said, harvesting does still have consequences for your kami.\u201d\nMENU: \u201cThe process of harvesting energy from a node has a slightly caustic effect on the energy of your kami\u2019s corporeal form.\u201d\nMENU: \u201cAs a kami harvests, its HP will slowly decrease. Over time, your kami\u2019s harvest rate will ramp up, and the rate of HP loss will ramp up with it.\u201d\nMENU: \u201cThis is very scary for a kami since it puts them at risk of being liquidated and having their corporeal form dissolved, but it\u2019s also when a kami is at their most productive.\u201d\nMENU: \u201cThe energy a kami harvests is called $MUSU. I\u2019ll explain more about it later.\u201d\nMENU: \u201cYou can wander around while your Kami harvest, but don\u2019t forget where you left them! Tired Kami are vulnerable to predators.\u201d\nMENU: \u201cDeploy your kami and do a little harvesting to get a feel for how it works.\u201d",
